{"conversationId": "d3e1cdd3-7eb8-44ce-b977-57a44d6fc602", "messageId": "1b534778-351c-4275-ae85-86bcd8cabd11", "userId": "ab832e40-0cab-4fb6-b9a6-52e3d1cbd3ce", "timestamp": "2026-01-27T06:56:10.113424+00:00", "status": "completed", "question": "How to create a binder with template?", "answer": "To create a binder using a template, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Access the Library**: Start by navigating to the Library and selecting \"All Library.\"\n\n2. **Create a Binder**:\n   - Click on the **+Create** button.\n   - From the dropdown menu, select **Binder** and click **Continue**.\n\n3. **Choose Binder Type**:\n   - On the Create Binder page, click in the **Choose binder type** box and select the appropriate binder type from the dropdown list.\n\n4. **Select a Template**:\n   - In the **Choose binder template** box, select the desired template for your binder.\n\n5. **Complete Required Metadata**:\n   - Fill in all required binder metadata. The required fields may vary based on the binder type and sub-type. Ensure to provide as much information as possible, as indicated by yellow fields.\n\n6. **Save the Binder**:\n   - After completing the necessary fields, click **Save**. You may also select the **Notify me when complete** checkbox if you wish to receive a notification once the binder is created.\n\n7. **Finalize Creation**: Click **OK** to finalize the creation of the binder.\n\nThis process will result in a binder that is pre-populated with multiple documents created from the selected templates, all in a Planned lifecycle state.\n\nSource: \"Create_Documents_from_Binder_Template.docx\", Page 3.", "doc_name": ["Create_Documents_from_Binder_Template.docx", "Create_Documents_from_Binder_GPS_Reports.docx", "Create_Edit_Binder.docx", "Create_Documents_from_Binder.docx"], "image_links": [{"image_name": "Create_Documents_from_Binder_Template_3_2.png", "image_url": "https://lly-data-ingestion-and-processing.s3.amazonaws.com/images/Create_Documents_from_Binder_Template_